\\ v &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,u=\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(\\pm 3,9).$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 3,\\,u^{2}\\le v\\le 9\\}.\n$$\n\n![](images/18/18c4c61a55dd2a361b82a208eb9a0d26f3fcfa213fe83b05f23644c9f79becaa.png)\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x}&\\frac{∂u}{∂y}\\\\\\frac{∂v}{∂x}&\\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{vmatrix}8&-2\\\\1&1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\right)}^{-1}=(10)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D dxdy &=\\iint_Δ |\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,dudv \\\\ &=\\iint_Δ |\\frac{1}{10}|\\,dudv \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{10}\\int_{-3}^{3}[\\int_{u^{2}}^{9}dv]du \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{10}\\int_{-3}^{3}[v]_{u^{2}}^{9}du \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{10}\\int_{-3}^{3}(9)-(u^{2})du \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{10}\\int_{-3}^{3}(9 - u^{2})du \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{10}[- \\frac{u^{3}}{3} + 9 u]_{-3}^{3} \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{10}(((27)+(-9))-((-27)+(9))) \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{10}(36) \\\\ &=\\frac{18}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "067912ba-31ed-5eca-bf1b-2e1a722add95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558853} {:answer/id #uuid "5dd8c0ca-63f1-573c-9fc6-3d6c2d297b5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answ